    "description": "Welcome to 669 44th Avenue, a one-of-a-kind Outer Richmond residence that marries timeless craftsmanship with modern luxury. Fully reimagined in 2018 by Sutro Architects and Pioneer Builders, with design by Marissa Thieriot of MGT Architectural Color, the home blends refined sensibilities with the vibrancy of beach life. Set against sweeping views of the Pacific Ocean & Golden Gate Park, the property offers every modern amenity. The designer kitchen features Italian terracotta floors, antique brass fixtures, farmhouse sink, custom cabinetry, Thermador appliances, and a walk-in pantry. Handcrafted stained glass, custom millwork, woven natural shades, and Marvin windows add character throughout. Upstairs, the primary suite offers ocean views, two custom walk-in closets, spa-like bath, and private deck. Two additional bedrooms share a Jack & Jill bath, while each of the three baths features distinctive wallpaper & Fireclay tile. The lower level includes a versatile garage/play space, laundry, and mudroom entry. Outdoors, enjoy views from decks on both levels, and Everdell-designed gardens showcase espaliered fruit trees, a large yard with natural grass, and a bluestone patio. Every detail from layered lighting to a surf-view camera system was crafted to be both beautiful & livable."
  },
